+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declared a booked visit immutable: neither changeable nor cancellable. The [2026-08-08 ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) confirmed that row as a deliberate decision rather than a survey artifact, and set the condition for reopening it — an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, never the request itself.
+
+The owner has now made that decision (2026-08-27). A visit booked with the wrong date or the wrong description can only be left wrong, because the sample deletes nothing (NG-4) and amends nothing. Forward-only correction is what the sample already demonstrates for owner details (REQ-OWN-004) and pet details (REQ-PET-004); a visit was the one record excluded from it.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the row bundles two capabilities with different costs. Cancellation needs a cancelled state; correction needs none.
+2. **Open NG-5 entirely.** Build correction and cancellation. Rejected: cancellation adds the lifecycle state the sample carries nowhere else, which is the original rationale and still holds.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, recorded as REQ-VIS-003. A correction replaces the visit's details in place; the pet gains no second visit record and no record of the earlier values is kept. Correction is checked against the same rules as booking.
+
+Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope. NG-5 is narrowed to cancellation alone and keeps its ID.
+
+The correction form carries no visible entry point in this decision: no page links to it, and whoever corrects a visit reaches the form by its address. This is recorded as NG-10, deferred rather than declined — a follow-up request may add a link.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample now demonstrates forward-only correction across all three record kinds: owner, pet, and visit. The 2026-08-08 statement that a booked visit is immutable no longer holds; that ADR's status names this narrowing.
+- Cancellation and deletion remain closed. NG-4 is untouched.
+- The future-date rule applies to a correction as it applies to a booking, and it constrains the submitted date only. A visit whose date has passed is therefore correctable, and correcting it reschedules that visit into the future. Recorded as an open question in the PRD; this behavior is the reading taken meanwhile.
+- NG-10 leaves the correction capability unreachable from the interface until a follow-up request. A capability with no entry point is testable but not discoverable, which is the accepted cost of splitting the two requests.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5, NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row and the added NG-10 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability the narrowing opens.
